+## Status of the branch (2026-09-09, evening: promoted for the multi-user profiles)
+
+`gfx906` = upstream master 2026-09-09 (5a4d0feca) merged into the mx-llama.cpp master of the same day (b9a990b28 + 4), plus the Exabit
+series (16 commits), the S1b a3 kernel (repacked Q8_0 narrow-batch mat-vec through 16 columns with width-dependent launch bounds), the
+MTP draft-graph `out_ids` fix, DPP warp reductions on GCN outside the flash-attention kernels (furnace 32f284244 + `GGML_GCN_NO_DPP` in
+`fattn-tile.cuh`/`fattn-vec.cuh`), the box's own head-256 single-stream tile row (64 threads, 64-row tiles), upstream PR 27210's
+adaptive MTP depth (`--spec-type draft-mtp-adaptive`, off by default), and `build.sh` compiling the FA kernels for the f16, q8_0 and
+q8_0-K/q4_0-V caches (`GGML_CUDA_FA_QUANTS`). Built as `/opt/llama.cpp-gfx906-20260909` (symlink `/opt/llama.cpp-gfx906`), tag
+`gfx906-20260909`. Measured against production (fork b10254 + the series) at 32K depth on the four-die box, two rounds
+(tuning guide `reports/2026-09-09-night-report.md`):
+
+| cell | production | this branch |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| four dies pp2048 / pp2048 @32K | 1130 / 776 | **1354 / 847** |
+| four dies tg128 / tg128 @32K | 57.4 / 54.3 | 55.0 / 53.5 |
+| one die pp512 / @32K | 311 / 214 | **424 / 274** |
+| one die tg128 / @32K | 20.7 / 18.05 | **22.6 / 20.08** |
+| batched 8 / 16 slots × 32K, decode | 141.6 / 160.4 | 141.5 / 159.4 |
+| server, 32K prompts, 8 / 16 clients, total tok/s | 811 / 717 | **929 / 802** (TTFT −15%) |
+| single user 32K, draft 3 | 73.7 | 65.2 |
+| perplexity 16K/6 | 5.5969 (its lineage) | 5.6099 (upstream's band) |
+| `test-backend-ops`, all ops | — | 16141/16141 |
+
+**Serves the multi-user profiles** (team, busy, pairs, ingest, batch in the tuning guide's `settings/launch.sh`); **production stays
+for the single-user MTP profiles** until candidate 2 (the one-column whole-block load on the two-plane layout) closes the one-token
+repacked-kernel gap (−4.5% plain, −11.5% with draft 3 at 32K). Things measured and not taken in the same night: alex4300's head-256
+tile rows (−8% single stream at depth, −5% batched at depth, +0.4% perplexity), DPP inside the attention kernels (−3.6% prefill at
+depth, −8% draft-3 verify). Note the `s1b-a` name is both a tag (the first, spilling form) and a branch (a3): merge `refs/heads/s1b-a`.
+
+**Reference perplexity** for Qwen3.8-27B Q8_0 at 16K/6 chunks is 5.61–5.62 on upstream since 2026-09-06 (5.5969 on the
 b10254/b10288 production lineage); the move is upstream's (`-funsafe-math-optimizations` removed 2026-08-12, then the GDN
 norm eps inside the root 2026-09-06; tuning guide `reports/2026-09-08-ppl-bisect.md`). Never read the 0.4% as a regression.
 
